  <section class="more" id="everything">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-h" data-reveal>
        <h2>The parts you only notice when they are missing</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Small things other players get almost right.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid" data-reveal style="--dl:1">
        <div class="cell">
          <svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-play"/></svg>
          <h3>On screen in half a second</h3>
          <p><b>0.56 s</b> from click to a usable window on an Apple Silicon Mac: nothing loads before you need it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cell">
          <svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-conf"/></svg>
          <h3>Live media info</h3>
          <p>Codec, resolution, audio layout and the real bitrate, refreshed every second while the panel is open.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cell">
          <svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-pip"/></svg>
          <h3>The window remembers where it was</h3>
          <p>Size and position come back at launch, or the window fits the video without leaving the screen.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cell">
          <svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-search"/></svg>
          <h3>The preview is the frame you land on</h3>
          <p>Seekbar thumbnails sharpen to the exact frame once the cursor stops, not the keyframe before it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cell">
          <svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-skip"/></svg>
          <h3>Skip intro that knows what an intro is</h3>
          <p>Chapters match by their whole title, so "Ending the war for good" is never taken for the credits.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cell">
          <svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-pip"/></svg>
          <h3>A mini player that stays put</h3>
          <p>Small, always on top and snapped to a corner. On macOS it floats over other apps in fullscreen.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cell">
          <svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-keys"/></svg>
          <h3>47 actions, all rebindable</h3>
          <p>Hotkeys follow physical keys, so they work in any keyboard layout. J, K and L do what you expect.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cell">
          <svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-hdr"/></svg>
          <h3>HDR, Dolby Vision, anything</h3>
          <p>Decoded by libmpv, as in mpv and IINA: full format coverage, hardware decoding and HDR tone mapping.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cell">
          <svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-loop"/></svg>
          <h3>A–B loops and frame steps</h3>
          <p>Loop the stretch between two marks, and step one frame forward or back.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cell">
          <svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-zoom"/></svg>
          <h3>Zoom and pan without a jump</h3>
          <p>Zoom and position change in the same frame, so the picture never jumps between two redraws.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cell">
          <svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-frame"/></svg>
          <h3>Export the frame you are on</h3>
          <p>Save or copy the exact decoded frame, HDR tone mapping included.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cell">
          <svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-audio"/></svg>
          <h3>Audio that behaves</h3>
          <p>Pick the output device, level a film that whispers then shouts, and keep an audio delay per file.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cell">
          <svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-queue"/></svg>
          <h3>The folder is the queue</h3>
          <p>The next episode starts after a countdown you can cancel. Repeat one file, the queue, or nothing.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cell">
          <svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-shield"/></svg>
          <h3>Folders that leave no trace</h3>
          <p>Mark a folder private and nothing about it is recorded or sent anywhere. There is no account, and the player reports one thing, once: that it was installed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cell">
          <svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-conf"/></svg>
          <h3>Your own mpv.conf still wins</h3>
          <p>Settings change only their own lines in mpv.conf, so options you wrote by hand survive.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cell spare" aria-hidden="true">
          <p>Oops — this square needed covering. Fifteen does not divide by two, so at this width the grid comes up one short. Widen the window and the corner goes away.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
